'''Infinity 0 Series''' (output) indexes the finished, human-edited stories and front matter from the
''Infinity 0'' input series. See the input page for the source-side sub-specification: raw, unedited
manuscript pages/stories this output is produced from. Renamed from ''Infinity 0'' to free that title up
for the book's title page, [[Infinity_0]] — the title page and the series share a name, so the series
page needed to move.

== Status ==

* '''State:''' title page landed ([[Infinity_0]]). No story has completed a human edit pass yet.
* '''Source:''' 495+ unedited pages/stories, unordered — see <code>mediawiki-input/Infinity_0</code>.
* '''Output types requested:''' per [[Infinity_0_Interview]] — LaTeX (publisher-ready print PDF, 5.5"
  x 8.5" trim), a static webpage (rich multimedia, linear, AI-generated audio/images), and a 3D model
  (concept-blockout scene/environment models, TypeScript + WebGL, static-hosted). None produced yet.

== Fan-out output types (interview result) ==

Per ''SPEC.md'''s "Fan-out", the LaTeX/webpage/3D-model outputs above are unlikely to be wiki-content-
shaped the way an edited story's plain text is — they'll most likely each get a link/index entry here
once produced, rather than being rendered inline. Not yet decided whether these three fan out directly
from the raw input, or downstream of the edited-text output below (chaining, per the idea in
<code>IDEAS.md</code>) — i.e. does [[The_Exceptional_Do-er]] work from the raw manuscript, or from the
human-edited result?

== Representation ==

An edited story is plain text, so it fits as wiki content directly — this is the "rendered result" case
from ''SPEC.md'''s "First concrete case", not the link case. As individual stories complete a human edit
pass, each one becomes its own output page here, filename as the story's title (spaces as underscores,
per the same convention as the input side).

This page itself is not a story — it's the index/placeholder for the series. Front matter and stories
share this same per-page convention: [[Infinity_0]] is the title page (front matter, not a story) —
title '''Infinity 0''', author '''Agent 0'''.

== Open questions ==

* '''Ordering''' — '''resolved''' per [[Infinity_0_Interview]]: each output type orders independently.
  It doesn't have to wait for or mirror an eventual order on the input side.
* '''Traceability''' — each per-story output page should trace back to which input page and which human
  edit pass produced it (<code>PRD.md</code> R8). Not yet decided how that link is recorded — on the
  output page itself, or elsewhere.
* '''Re-editing''' — if a story gets a second human edit pass later, does that replace this page's
  content, or does history need to be kept somewhere?

